<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hormizd IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 590</span> · Also known as Hormozd IV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hormizd IV was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> from 579 to 590. Son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a>, he waged wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> and the Turks, and around 580 he abolished the monarchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, governing it through a Persian official. His conflict with the nobility and with his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahram-chobin">Bahram Chobin</a> led to his deposition and murder in 590, after which his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> took the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hormizd-iv.jpg" alt="Hormizd IV" width="255" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drachma_of_Hormidz_IV_-_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
